MAXUSAI 906: carry upstream's revert of "restore prop.integrated on HIP builds".

Upstream llama.cpp PR #28604 (d4389a4dd92, 2026-09-08T14:19:53Z) reverts
c7d8722922a (#24233), which set info.devices[id].integrated = prop.integrated on
HIP builds. On an integrated/UMA device that flag changes which buffer types the
HIP backend claims, and upstream issue #28211 root-causes the result as an MMQ
tile-barrier race on gfx115x that produces WRONG OUTPUT with no crash and no
warning, once a decode exceeds n_ubatch.

WE MISSED THE FIX BY 78 MINUTES. Our payload b10864 is 5d806aa25, 2026-09-08
13:01:03Z. The revert landed at 14:19:53Z the same day, so ollama v0.34.1 has the
defect and not the fix.

MEASURED HERE (gfx1151, Radeon 8060S, ROCm 7.2.x), gemma4:31b-it-q4_K_M with the
image-token budget pinned per cell, name_bbox_mean_iou:

    budget   0.32.1/b9888   0.34.1/b10864
       280       0.612          0.691
       560       0.713          0.714
      1120       0.728          0.000   <-- total loss

Only the top rung fails, and only on the newer payload. prompt_eval_count is
identical between builds on every test, so the grid and token count are unchanged
and the pixels reaching the model are the same -- consistent with corruption
downstream of preprocessing rather than in it. Related upstream reports on this
exact silicon: #27419 (upper image content lost on HIP, Vulkan and CPU correct)
and #28211 (wrong logits past n_ubatch).

GGML_CUDA_NO_PINNED=1 is NOT a workaround: it reaches the runner and the runner
aborts (signal: aborted, core dumped) on model load.

Drop this patch when the payload advances past d4389a4dd92.

